  "raw": {
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Kitchen-Assistant_R-0000003425": {
      "title": "Kitchen Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nJob no: R-0000003425 Position Title: Kitchen Assistant Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Full time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 08/24/2026 Job Description: Mount Holyoke College Dining Commons offers a diverse array of cuisines tailored to meet various dietary preferences and needs. Our menu frequently rotates to provide students, faculty, and staff with an expansive selection. Highlights include the customizable WOK station, offering personalized stir fry dishes, and the Baraka station, specializing is Halal cuisine. For those seeking Kosher options, the L’Chaim station is available. Our culinary team is dedicated to crafting nutritious, flavorful meals that cater to the diverse tastes of our students, faculty, and staff. We prioritize safety and sanitation in all meal preparations. In addition to Vegan and Vegetarian options, we strive to create an inclusive dining environment where every person, despite their dietary needs, can enjoy healthy and delicious foods. Essential Functions: Operating and maintaining dish machines according to proper procedures. Washing all pots, pans and utensils, cleans up the dish return area, dining rooms and service areas following proper health and sanitation practices. Recording accurate Time & Temp logs along with proper PH balance of sanitizers in pot sinks and dish machines. Washing all tables and chairs as needed, mops floors between meal periods or as needed, emptying trash and compost in proper receptacles. Emptying grease trap catch screens and keeping them clean. Keeping all work areas clean, free of debris and sanitized at all times. Maintaining the flow of dishes, silverware, pots, pans so they don’t get backed up and delivering them back to their designated areas. At times, will provide direction, supervision, and training to student staff and must maintain a high level of professionalism. Assists in putting away food orders and deliveries as needed. Working with others, including students, as well as work alone without supervision. Qualifications: Good communication skills, both written and orally. General knowledge of food and operation of kitchen/dish room equipment. Ability to pass a physical examination without restrictions. Ability to lift/move an average of 50 pounds without restrictions. Willingness to participate in a ServSafe class to obtain Food Protection Manager Certification. Ability to maintain an extraordinarily positive attitude in dealing with students and the public. Ability to work cooperatively and give direction to others. Must comply with safety and sanitation regulations as prescribed by law. Must comply with proper dress code as designated by the Department. Entry Rate $20.43 - Working Rate $21.77 Dining Video Please note that this position falls under a Union, which ensures fair compensation and benefits for all employees. What We Offer: Our comprehensive benefits program offers a range of options to you can make choices that work best for you and your family: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Cook_R-0000003723": {
      "title": "Cook",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJob no: R-0000003723 Position Title: Cook Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Full time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $28.76 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 11/16/2026 Job Description: Mount Holyoke College Dining Commons offers a diverse array of cuisines tailored to meet various dietary preferences and need.  Our menu frequently rotates to provide students, faculty, and staff with an expansive selection.  Highlights include the customizable WOK station, offering personalized stir0fry dishes, and the Baraka station, specializing is Halal cuisine.  For those seeking Kosher options, the L’Chaim station is available. Our culinary team is dedicated to crafting nutritious, flavorful meals that cater to the diverse tastes of our students, faculty, and staff.  We prioritize safety and sanitation in All meal preparations.  In addition to Vegan and Vegetarian options, we strive to create an inclusive dining environment where every person, despite their dietary needs can enjoy healthy and delicious foods. This is a 34-week academic year position, running from September through May. Please note that services may not be required during periods when school is not in session.     Essential Job Functions: As a Cook, you will operate under the supervision of the Chef Manager, Lead Cook, Executive Chef, Associate Director of Culinary Operations, and Dining Managers.  Your primary responsibilities include: Preparation of recipes while ensuring safe handling and proper food preparation techniques. Adherence to sanitation and Board of Health (BOH) regulations, including proper receiving and storage procedures. Record daily temperatures of all food items and maintain production records to ensure food safety, compliance with BOH regulations. Complete administrative tasks such as providing accurate information for menu planning and inventory management on a daily basis. Comply with the proper dress code designated by the Dining Department an be neat in appearance and work habits to comply with safety and sanitation regulations. Collaboration with culinary team members to facilitate smooth and efficient operations. Food preparation using methods such as boiling, roasting, sautéing, steaming, baking, frying, and grilling/broiling. Customization of meals to accommodate customer preferences and dietary restrictions. Assurance of accurate allergen information and ingredient labeling. Consistent use of standardized recipes to maintain food quality and presentation. Batch cooking to minimize waste and ensure fresh food availability. Implementation of inventory management practices, including regular inventory counts and First in, First out (FIFO) method utilization. Proper maintenance of cooking equipment and up-keep a clean and organized workspace. Display a positive and cooperative attitude while maintain a strong work ethic. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change or new ones may be assigned at any time with or without notice. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum 2 years of experience in high-volume food preparation. Ability to pass a pre-employment physical examination without restrictions. Must possess strong written and verbal communication skills, along with a proficient understanding of the English language. ServSafe certification or willingness to obtain certification. Certification in allergen training or willingness to obtain one. Commitment to exceptional customer service and professionalism Preferred Qualifications: Preference of 3 years of experience in high-volume food preparation, preferably in a higher education setting or quality restaurant setting. Proficiency in basic computer skills Hiring Range: $28.76-$30.66 Please note that this position falls under a Union, which ensures fair compensation and benefits for all employees. What We Offer: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9.5% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Dining Video Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Five-College-Astronomy-Department-Fellow_R-0000003668": {
      "title": "Five College Astronomy Department Fellow",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nJob no: R-0000003668 Position Title: Five College Astronomy Department Fellow Work Type: Faculty   Full time   In-Person Start Date: 07/01/2027 Job Description: The Five College Astronomy Department (FCAD), which consists of Amherst, Hampshire, Mount Holyoke, Smith College and the University of Massachusetts, invites applications for a three-year teaching and research postdoctoral fellowship, to be based at Mount Holyoke College, with a tentative start date of July 1, 2027. The successful candidate must be dedicated to undergraduate education and have experience mentoring students who are broadly diverse with regard to race, ethnicity, socioeconomic status, gender, nationality, sexual orientation, disability, and religion. Candidates from groups underrepresented in astronomy are encouraged to apply. The educational component will consist of teaching two undergraduate classes per academic year, of which at least one will be in observational astronomy, including leading a one-week observing trip to a professional observatory in Arizona. The second course may also be in observational science or another area of interest to the candidate. The fellow is also expected to conduct a strong research program that is synergistic with existing research in the FCAD and that has potential for undergraduate contributions. The FCAD provides multiple opportunities for research collaborations. For example, applicants will have the opportunity to participate in science projects with the Large Millimeter Telescope in Mexico. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in astronomy, planetary science, physics, or a closely-related field, and should submit (1) a cover letter; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a statement of research goals and a proposal for a research project that would be conducted during your time in the FCAD; (4) a statement of teaching philosophy, including an indication of what you would offer to the planned observational astronomy course(s) and a second possible course. Reference letters will be requested at a later date in the process. Review of applications will begin January 1, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. Details about the Mount Holyoke College Department of Physics & Astronomy can be found here and the Five College Astronomy Department can be found here . Minimum starting rate of pay: $65,000.   Mount Holyoke is an undergraduate liberal arts college with 2,200 students and 220 faculty. Mount Holyoke College is located about 90 miles west of Boston in the Connecticut River valley, and is a member of the Five College Consortium consisting of Amherst, Hampshire, Mount Holyoke, and Smith Colleges and the University of Massachusetts.   Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
