    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Lyons-Lift-Driver_R-0000003537": {
      "title": "Lyons Lift Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-28\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003537 Position Title: Lyons Lift Driver Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $21.87 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 09/28/2026 Job Description: Lyons Lift drivers support individuals with permanent or temporary mobility limitations with rides on campus, ensuring them safe and friendly access to classes, dining, and other campus locations, as well as the Village Commons. Driver shifts start at 7:45am through the early afternoon Mondays through Thursdays throughout the semester. Shifts are primarily spent in the van providing rides based on the schedule for that day as well as fielding calls to schedule additional rides as-needed. Primary responsibilities include safe operation of vehicles on shift, effective management of ride scheduling, knowledge of campus pickup locations, comfort working with people with disabilities, and maintaining a helpful, kind, and safety-forward attitude while engaging with student riders. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Ensure the safe transportation of individuals on route Assist individuals entering and exiting the vehicle as needed Possess knowledge of relevant ADA guidelines and familiarity with ramp deployment and wheelchair securement technology Provide curb-to-curb service in a professional, safe, and courteous manner Conduct and document vehicle safety checks before each shift Maintain punctuality for rides on shift Manage scheduling with passengers during shifts Report and record all incidents to Public Safety Dispatch and document for the Lyons Lift Supervisor Maintain confidentiality and professionalism Keep vehicle clean and free of trash Record daily ridership records Communicate with the direct supervisor any issues or concerns Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications: You must be a fleet-certified driver or able to become certified Valid driver’s license (any state) and satisfactory driving record (no violations within the last year) Satisfactory criminal background check and drug/alcohol screen may be required Embraces and actively promotes an inclusive and equitable environment for all members of the MHC community Ability to work in a fast-paced environment. Call volume can be very high before and after classes, as well as during bad weather Preferred Qualifications: Excellent interpersonal skills, pleasant and friendly demeanor Demonstrates ability to work independently Experience working with people with disabilities and people with mobility limitations. Demonstrates skill in understanding cultural differences Strengthens Mount Holyoke College’s climate for inclusion and acceptance Embraces and actively promotes an includes and equitable work environment Hiring Range: $21.87 - $24.05 Full Job Description What We Offer: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Music-Instructor_R-0000003532": {
      "title": "Music Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003532 Position Title: Music Instructor Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $0.00 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: Job Description: The Mount Holyoke College Department of Music seeks Music Instructors to teach Individual Performance Study (ie. music lessons) for interested students. Instructors are on the active roster for lessons in their instrument(s), though the total number of billable teaching hours each semester is subject, as always, to student enrollments. Our Music Instructors teach students at all levels, from beginner to advanced, across a range of voice types and instruments. Individual Performance Study is one of the requirements for the Music major, supports excellence in our many department ensembles, and is also very popular with non-majors/minors. Lessons are one of the few instructional areas where a student can experience sustained one-on-one teaching, and may have the same instructor each semester for their entire undergraduate career. We therefore prize Music Instructors who cultivate welcoming, respectful, and supportive studios; offer students a diverse range of repertoire; prioritize wellness and sustainable approaches to technique; and help students develop pathways for a lifetime of thoughtful engagement with music, whatever their future professional goals may be. This is an academic-year, non-benefited appointment (September 1 - May 31), renewable annually.  Important Application Note: This is a Rolling Application. We are continuously recruiting talent for our future needs. Submitting an application puts your information directly into our active pool, and we will contact you for an interview should a suitable opening become available. Submitting an application does not guarantee an opening. Instruments currently offered: Piano Voice Flute Oboe Clarinet Saxophone Bassoon French Horn Trumpet - Currently Searching for Trumpet Instructor (for AY26-27) Trombone Tuba Percussion Harpsichord Organ Harp Guitar Electric Guitar Violin Viola Cello Double Bass Electric Bass Early instruments: Lute, Viola da Gamba, Recorders, etc. Essential Responsibilities: Offer 10 30-minute or 60-minute lessons per student per semester, depending on the number of credits and student enrollments Assist students with placement and enrollment Prepare and distribute syllabi Prepare for lessons Assist students in preparing for end-of-semester performances and half or full recitals Assist students with mentorship and musical opportunities as appropriate Submit grades Qualifications: Master’s degree in Music Minimum one year prior experience teaching one-on-one private music lessons Commitment to Mount Holyoke College’s climate of academic excellence and inclusive learning within our gender-diverse women’s liberal arts college environment Compensation: $ 73.54/HR for lessons and $36.78/HR for administrative work Special Instructions for Applicants: Apply online; application materials must include: A cover letter summarizing interests and qualifications A complete resume or curriculum vitae Links to at least two videos of you in performance for each instrument you teach, recorded within the last 5 years Encouraged but not required: one or more videos of you teaching your instrument, recorded within the last 5 years Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Stable-Assistant_R-0000003243": {
      "title": "Stable Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-20\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003243 Position Title: Stable Assistant Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $21.87 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 10/05/2026 Job Description: The Stable Assistant supports the daily operations of the Mount Holyoke College Equestrian Center by providing high-quality care for horses and maintaining the cleanliness, safety, and organization of the stables. This role is essential in fostering a welcoming and professional environment for students, boarders, and visitors, while ensuring the health and well-being of the college’s equine partners. Schedule: Wednesday: 10AM-6PM Saturday: 10AM-6PM Sunday: 10AM-6PM Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Essential Worker (all weather and holidays) Provide hay and fresh water to horses Feed horses according to individualized grain cards and administer supplements Track supplement inventory and notify boarders or stable manager when supplies are low Turn out and bring in horses on a rotational schedule Clean and maintain horse stalls (10–13 daily, with occasional additional needs) Sweep aisles, remove debris, and maintain a tidy appearance throughout the barn Clean and maintain wash stalls, drains, and water tubs Remove trash and replace bags Conduct regular cobwebbing and dusting Move and organize feed, hay, and bedding as needed Muck paddocks and rake hay or leaves from surrounding areas Operate barn equipment such as tractors and manure wagons Assist with regular maintenance projects and seasonal preparations Examples: dragging arenas, raking walkways, dusting knee-walls, and prepping for returning boarders Work collaboratively with other barn staff to ensure smooth daily operations Read the Stable log and check the Daily staff schedule before every shift Communicate regularly with the associate director regarding horse care and facility needs Required Qualifications: Previous horse handling, husbandry, and general farm experience. Must be able to work both independently as well as on a team. Ability to operate and learn google sheets and forms. Preferred Qualifications: Experience operating a tractor and farm equipment. Experience with dragging an arena and general arena maintenance. Equine first aid and emergency knowledge. Experience working at an equine boarding facility Experience working in a lesson barn. Hiring Range: $ 21.87 - $24.05 What We Offer: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/PTOC-Lyons-Lift-Driver_R-0000003494": {
      "title": "PTOC Lyons Lift Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-03\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003494 Position Title: PTOC Lyons Lift Driver Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $19.50 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 08/24/2026 Job Description: Part Time On-Call Driver for Lyons Lift, Mount Holyoke's on-campus accessible ride program The Lyons Lift program at Mount Holyoke College is looking for a part time on-call employee to join our team at Public Safety and Services . Lyons Lift Drivers operate our wheelchair accessible van to support individuals with permanent or temporary mobility limitations with rides on campus, ensuring them safe and friendly access to classes, dining, and other campus locations, as well as the Village Commons. In this role, you would be asked to work coverage shifts as needed and for special events. Ensure the safe transportation of individuals on route  Assist individuals entering and exiting the vehicle as needed Provide curb-to-curb service in a professional, safe, and courteous manner Conduct and document vehicle safety checks before each shift Manage scheduling with passengers during shifts  Report and record all incidents to Public Safety Dispatch and document for the Lyons Lift Supervisor. Maintain confidentiality and professionalism Keep vehicle clean and free of trash Record daily ridership records Communicate with the direct supervisor any issues or concerns Qualifications: You must be a fleet-certified driver or able to become certified  Valid driver’s license (any state) and satisfactory driving record (no violations within the last year)  Ability to work in a fast-paced environment. Call volume can be very high before and after classes, as well as during bad weather  Ability to assist individuals in and out of vehicles Excellent interpersonal skills, pleasant and friendly demeanor Ability to communicate effectively with riders and supervisors  Demonstrated ability to work independently Must be available to attend all meetings and training sessions Satisfactory criminal background check and drug/alcohol screen may be required All drivers and riders must wear seat belts. No cell phone usage or any other distractions while driving  Safety check of the vehicle before and after each shift.  Ability to safely refuel the vehicle at MHC pump Full Job Description Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Club-Sports-Coach---Part-Time_R-0000003028": {
      "title": "Club Sports Coach - Part-Time",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-07\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003028 Position Title: Club Sports Coach - Part-Time Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $20.00 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 08/01/2026 Job Description: Mount Holyoke College’s Athletics Department is seeking part-time Club Coaches to guide our dedicated student-athletes. This is more than just coaching; it’s fostering athletic excellence, leadership development, and personal growth within a collaborative club sports environment. If you have a passion for your sport and a commitment to mentorship, this is your chance to coach a team of motivated, bright student leaders. Important Application Note: This is a Rolling Application. We are continuously recruiting talent for our future needs. Submitting an application puts your information directly into our active pool, and we will contact you for an interview should a suitable opening becomes available. Submitting an application does not guarantee an immediate opening. Why be a Club Coach at MHC? You’ll be a direct mentor to exceptional student athletes, helping them shape their athletic and leadership journeys. This role requires approximately 6-8 hours per week during the academic year, primarily during weekday evenings. It’s the perfect opportunity for local experts, recent graduates, or passionate individuals seeking involvement outside of a standard 9-to-5. You'll work closely with student-run club boards, collaborating on decisions and fostering an inclusive team culture. Club Sports currently offered:  Fencing Rugby Ultimate Frisbee Ice Hockey - Currently Searching for Head & Assistant Club Coaches Squash Dressage Western Essential Duties and Responsibilities:  Designing and executing engaging, high-quality practices focused on fundamentals, strategy, conditioning, and safety. Mentoring student leaders and collaborating with them on team vision and day-to-day decisions. Championing an inclusive team culture that supports the holistic growth (academic, athletic, and personal) of every student-athlete. Ensuring safety by supervising drills, maintaining equipment, and upholding all facility and departmental policies. Supporting the team at all practices and competitions (potential weeknight and weekend flexibility required). Listed as the PE Club Course Instructor and certify PE credits in collaboration with the Assistant Athletic Director. Qualifications: Proven experience playing and/or coaching your sport. Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills – you can clearly teach a technique and motivate a group. A commitment to diversity and inclusion and the ability to support an environment where all student-athletes feel valued. Familiarity with the rules, trends, and compliance requirements within your sport. Must be able to work weeknights/weekends as needed and possess a valid driver’s license. Hiring Range: $20.00 - $30.00/hr. Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Junior-Waitstaff_R-0000003132": {
      "title": "Junior Waitstaff",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-02-27\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003132 Position Title: Junior Waitstaff Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $18.00 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 04/01/2026 Job Description: The Willits-Hallowell Center and Events Services Department is seeking Junior Waitstaff to provide quality service to all guests of Mount Holyoke College. Those in this role are responsible for quality, timely, courteous, and efficient service to guests, adhering to the standards established by management. Essential Responsibilities:  Set up, serve, and clean both on-premise and off-premise functions. Lift and carry trays weighing up to 30 pounds to and from dining areas. Set up, refresh, and service meeting rooms with refreshments and linens as needed. Clean up at the conclusion of meetings and events. Occasional assistance in setting up function rooms, which involves moving tables and chairs, either within a room or to another location. Pack, load, and unload Catering vehicles. Work independently, exercise sound judgment, and exhibit initiative in performing daily duties. Complete opening and closing shift side work. Keep work areas and equipment clean and organized. Communicate effectively with guests and co-workers. Read and interpret event orders to determine set-up, service needs, and other duties the manager assigns. Required Qualifications:  Strong written and oral communication skills, with a sound understanding of the English language. Ability to maintain an extraordinarily positive attitude towards others, especially when dealing with students and the public. Must be cooperative and willing to work with others. Maintain a high level of professionalism. Preferred Qualifications:  Basic computer skills are desirable. Physical Demands:  Ability to lift 30 lbs. without aid. Ability to routinely lift, bend, twist and stand for the majority of up to an 8-hour shift. Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Executive-Assistant_R-0000003768": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nJob no: R-0000003768 Position Title: Executive Assistant Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Full time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $35.72 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 01/04/2027 Job Description: The Executive Assistant is an important member of the Office of the President’s administrative team. Reporting to the Special Assistant/Operations Manager, the Executive Assistant has primary responsibility for managing the President’s schedule and executing front-of-office operations. This is a fully in-person position with occasional nights and weekends required. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Management of the President’s Schedule The President’s time is one of the College’s most important resources. The Executive Assistant has primary responsibility for the President’s complex daily schedule, under the supervision of the Special Assistant/Operations Manager. The Executive Assistant: Understands the President’s priorities and preferred working rhythm, and uses that understanding to e xercise initiative and independent judgment in managing the President’s extremely busy schedule. Continually revises the calendar, facilitating the frequent changes required and responding to invitations and meeting requests in a timely manner. Proactively ensures accuracy and completeness of calendar  Ensures that all relevant information is included in the calendar, and that the calendar is correct. Ensures that briefing materials from other offices have been received in advance and reviews them for completeness and accuracy. Solicits tardy materials. For particularly important meetings/events, submits briefing materials to the Special Assistant/Operations Manager for an additional level of review. Works with the Special Assistant/Operations Manager to ensure that the President’s role in events organized by other offices is clear and appropriate. Books and manages the President’s travel arrangements.  Front-of-Office Operations The Executive Assistant is a key contact for College constituents both internal and external. The Executive Assistant: P romotes a positive image of Mount Holyoke College by fielding telephone calls and welcoming visitors to the President's office. Maintain a positive, personable and respectful demeanor. Responds to inquiries from diverse College constituencies (e.g., students, families, faculty, staff, trustees, alums, donors, public and private officials and community members), listening respectfully to constituent concerns; providing accurate information regarding College policies, decisions, programs, and events; referring inquiries or problems to the appropriate office or person; resolving problems as they are able; and keeping an updated log of critical calls. Ensures that visitors to the office are treated hospitably, the visitor’s reception area is well-kept, and that the kitchenette is stocked to accommodate visitor requests.  Maintains the physical space of the office and follows opening and/or closing procedures. Event Support Under the direction of the Special Assistant/Operations Manager and the Director of Presidential College Events, the Executive Assistant supports several events. Duties include: Handling logistics associated with College programs and events and/or meetings of the board of trustees as directed by the Special Assistant/Operations Manager, including scheduling rooms, making travel arrangements, following up with the College’s events staff, and processing invoices and reimbursements. Supporting major College/presidential events, including Convocation and Commencement. Assisting with other presidential events, including printing table cards and nametags, sending invitations and tracking rsvps. Additional Duties Under the direction of the Special Assistant/Operations Manager, the Executive Assistant also supports office operations. Duties include: Providing administrative support to the vice president/secretary of the College, including scheduling and providing technical support for meetings Monitoring the president’s public email account, referring messages that need attention to the special assistant/operations manager and ensuring that any needed follow-up has been completed. Receiving non-confidential written correspondence, determining next steps according to established procedures, and tracking the status of a reply as necessary. Ordering and restocking office supplies. Submitting and tracking Facilities Management work orders. Implementing the records management system under the direction of the special assistant/operations manager. In partnership with the office of communications, ensuring that the president’s office and board of trustee websites are up to date. Maintains Board of Trustees directory information; updates board list-servs, drives, documents, and electronic portal annually or as needed. Completing clerical tasks, such as creating contact reports in Salesforce and verifying purchases in Workday. Completing other special projects as assigned. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Hold an Associates Degree and have at least two years’ experience heavy scheduling in a fast-paced administrative environment, or a combination of equivalent education/professional experience. Have knowledge about and passion for women’s colleges and gender affirming communities. Maintain a professional demeanor at all times in a quiet office environment. Exhibit tact and discretion. Exercise good judgment and maintain strict confidentiality. Exhibit strong written and verbal communication skills. Work as part of a team as well as independently on a wide variety of projects. Prioritize work duties, and manage time effectively. Multi-task and transition quickly between tasks to address specific situations. Stay flexible as plans change. Manage multiple, concurrent tasks while continuing to meet deadlines. Work effectively under pressure, and with accuracy and attention to detail. Maintain effective, professional, and cooperative working relationships to collaborate successfully with other college departments and offices. Uphold the College’s commitment to diversity, equity and inclusion. Interact professionally with a diverse community of trustees, faculty, staff, students and alums. Understand clerical office procedures and have skills in operating standard office equipment. Understand and apply pertinent College rules, regulations, policies, and procedures in the course of carrying out their role. Preferred Qualifications: Have experience with Workday, Salesforce, Google Suite, Microsoft Suite, and Adobe Acrobat, or similar programs. Have previously worked in higher education or another non-profit environment. Have experience in executive support and/or hospitality. Hiring Range: $35.72 - $40.17 / Hour Full Job Description What We Offer: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Part-Time-On-Call-Van-Driver_R-0000003792": {
      "title": "Part Time On Call Van Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003792 Position Title: Part Time On Call Van Driver Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $19.89 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 12/01/2026 Job Description: The Facilities Management department at Mount Holyoke College is seeking a responsible and professional Part-Time On-Call Driver . Our department supports the entire campus community by maintaining over 2,000,000 square feet of property in 60+ major buildings and over 300 acres. The Part-Time On-Call Driver will be responsible for operating college-owned vehicles, including 7 and 12-passenger vans, to support a variety of college-sponsored events and activities, both on and off campus. This is an on-call position, with hours scheduled on an as-needed basis. Key Duties and Responsibilities: Drive college-owned vehicles for college-sponsored activities as scheduled. Assignments may include, but are not limited to, Department transportation, airport shuttles or off-campus trips. Occasional overnight trips may be required. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Valid Commonwealth of Massachusetts Driver’s license is required. Must possess an excellent driving record. Must demonstrate superior judgment and drive with utmost care. Must maintain a professional demeanor and provide excellent customer service at all times. Ability to travel for occasional overnight trips is essential. Must successfully complete the College’s driver credentialing program. Must provide a copy of RMV driving record. Hire Rate: $19.89 Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
