    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Dispatcher--Campus-Safety_R-0000003806": {
      "title": "Dispatcher, Campus Safety",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nJob no: R-0000003806 Position Title: Dispatcher, Campus Safety Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Full time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $24.05 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 11/16/2026 Job Description: Adhering to the principles of community engagement and community-oriented problem solving, the Dispatcher provides the initial point of contact for emergency response to criminal activity, fires, medicals, fire alarms, and many service-related calls. The Dispatcher also provides service to a diverse community as the college's operator. This is a 40 hour position, shifts are Sun/Mon 3pm-11pm and Thu/Fir/Sat 7am-3pm (Off Tuesday/Wednesday) Essential Job Duties:  Promptly answers emergency lines, business lines, and multiple college operator lines. Collects information from a diverse set of calling parties as well as walk-ins to the station in a timely manner and disseminates that information to the appropriate entities. Utilizes the National Crime Information Center and Criminal Justice Information System to respond to requests for information from on-duty police officers. Monitors fire, intrusion, panic, other alarms, and cameras on campus. Activates the college's emergency mass notification system as directed. Provides emergency instructions, calls in personnel after hours, and supports and assists the diverse community as a whole in a supportive and professional manner. Records details in the computer-aided dispatch software (IMC) database, information in which is often highly confidential, sensitive in nature, and protected by law. Review logs, postings, training, emails, CJIS output at the beginning and throughout shift. Assist officers with community engagement activities. Dispatches emergency and non-emergency incidents requiring fire, medical, or police response according to priority and availability of units. Qualifications: HS Diploma or Equivalent Related experience in law enforcement, security, or dispatching Strong problem-solving, time-management, and communication skills Ability to work in a fast-paced, multitasked environment. Sensitivity to issues of confidentiality Commitment to, experience with, and/or ability to work effectively with a broad spectrum of individuals from a variety of diverse backgrounds Preferred Qualifications: Certifications in CPR, CJIS, or APCO Experience in Public Safety Dispatching Minimum starting hourly rate for this position is $24.05 This role is classified under Hourly Grade 6H with an hourly range between $24.05 - $26.47 per hour. What We Offer: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Hotel-Manager_R-0000003784": {
      "title": "Hotel Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nJob no: R-0000003784 Position Title: Hotel Manager Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Full time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $78,342.00 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 11/16/2026 Job Description: The Hotel Manager will oversee the day-to-day operations of the Willits-Hallowell Conference Center & Hotel, ensuring efficient operations, strong financial performance, and a high level of guest service. Responsibilities include managing and developing hotel staff; overseeing budgets, revenue, billing, and reconciliation; monitoring inventory and placing vendor orders; and maintaining operational standards and procedures. The Hotel Manager will work closely with Event Services, College departments, clients, vendors, and guests to coordinate hotel operations for conferences, meetings, and other events. The position will develop strategies to increase overnight bookings, group business, occupancy, and revenue; address guest and operational concerns; and identify opportunities to improve efficiency and service. The Hotel Manager will also support the integration of hotel operations with the College’s broader hospitality and Event Services programs while fostering strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Manage daily operations of the Willits-Hallowell Conference Center & Hotel. Oversee and maintain the property management, point-of-sale, reservation, and credit card systems. Manage hotel inventory levels and place orders with vendors and suppliers as needed to ensure adequate supplies, amenities, linens, housekeeping products, guest room items, and other operational necessities are available.  Develop and implement policies and procedures for hotel operations. Greet guests, answer questions, and resolve issues regarding hotel services, amenities, and policies. Recruit, hire, train, and supervise personnel across multiple areas including front desk  and housekeeping. Create staff schedules, organize activities, and assign responsibilities to ensure productivity and high-quality guest service. Monitor employee performance and conduct regular evaluations to foster professional growth. Implement safety protocols, ensuring compliance with health and safety regulations and conducting regular inspections. Responsible for collecting payments, tracking revenue, and maintaining records of budgets, funds, and expenses. Oversee financial activities including establishing room rates, setting budgets, analyzing sales figures, and identifying opportunities to improve hotel revenue and profitability. Manage the Financial Consulting Specialist, ensuring the accuracy and timeliness of hotel billing, invoicing, account reconciliation, financial reporting, and related financial processes. Partner with the Sales Manager to develop targeted marketing and business development initiatives designed to increase overnight hotel bookings, attract new group and individual business, and drive hotel revenue. Work closely with Event Services, Sales, and external clients to coordinate events with overnight accommodations from initial planning through guest departure, including room blocks, guest services, arrival and departure logistics, and other hotel-related needs. . Complete and monitor payroll and associated duties. Coordinate with external parties, including suppliers, contractors, conference planners, and other service providers. Work in collaboration with Event Services to ensure events and conferences run smoothly. Provide operational support, staffing coordination, guest services, logistics, and on-site management for large-scale events (e.g. Commencement, Reunion, Family Weekend) as needed, including responsibilities that extend beyond the day-to-day operation of the hotel. Work collaboratively across Hospitality Services and other College departments to ensure the hotel and Event Services operations support the overall goals and priorities of the College. Supervise maintenance work, renovations, and furnishings as needed. Other duties as assigned Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in hospitality, business administration, or a relevant field. A minimum of 5 years experience in hotel management or a similar role. Exceptional ability to communicate effectively and professionally, both verbally and in writing, with all College constituents. Must be able to demonstrate creative and strategic thinking, problem-solving skills, and strength in handling difficult conversations with diplomacy and ease. Must have strong computer proficiency including Microsoft Office and Google suites. Ability to learn new software programs essential to performing responsibilities. Strong understanding of hotel management best practices and data entry software. Positive, constructive attitude with a drive to provide exemplary customer service to internal and external constituents. Initiative and ability to work independently. Supervisory experience. Alternatives to formal education and paid work experience may be considered as equivalent qualifications to include military service/training, volunteering, activism, and other non-traditional programs and experiences related to the position. Supervision: Front desk staff (professional and student)  Housekeeping staff (professional and student)  Financial Consulting Specialist Hiring Range: $78,342 - 90,093 Full Job Description What We Offer: 403(b) Retirement Plan (College contributes 9% of salary) Comprehensive medical, dental and vision insurance Flexible Spending Account (FSA) Disability and Leave Benefits Life Insurance (College paid coverage 1x salary) Employee Assistance Program Tuition Benefits (to Mount Holyoke College or others) Generous Paid Time Off Access to Kendall Sports & Dance Complex Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    },
    "https://mtholyoke.wd504.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Mount-Holyoke-College---Main-Campus/Interim-Music-Instructor---Klezmer-Ensemble_R-0000003710": {
      "title": "Interim Music Instructor - Klezmer Ensemble",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nJob no: R-0000003710 Position Title: Interim Music Instructor - Klezmer Ensemble Faculty or Staff: Staff Full Time or Part Time: Part time In-Person, Hybrid, or Remote: In-Person Minimum Starting Rate of Pay: $73.54 Rate of pay commensurate with experience Start Date: 01/18/2027 Job Description: Interim Music Instructor - Klezmer Ensemble The Mount Holyoke College Department of Music seeks an interim Music Instructor to lead the Klezmer Ensemble in Spring 2027 as a one-semester sabbatical replacement. Open to all instrumentalists, this ensemble specializes in the dance music of Eastern Europe, learning the historical, ornamental, and improvisatory approaches to this musical tradition. The Klezmer Ensemble is open to instrumentalists at all levels via a no-fear audition, particularly clarinets, flutes, strings, and brass, plus one keyboardist and percussionist. The position requires knowledge of klezmer scores and  all instruments so as to work with students on ways to stylistically learn suggested tunes using a lead sheet format, formatted for Bb, C, Eb, + bass clef. Chosen repertoire will be worked on harmonically as well as each tune will be presented with component historical or biographical information. The Ensemble regularly rehearses on Wednesdays 5:00-6:30, and the Spring concert is tentatively scheduled for Wednesday, April 28, 2027 at 5:30-7:00pm.  This is a non-benefited appointment, paid hourly per rehearsal. This role has an hourly rate of $73.54 for teaching/performance and and hourly rateof $36.78 for admin/rehearsal Special Instructions for Applicants: Apply online; application materials must include: A cover letter summarizing interests and qualifications A complete resume or curriculum vitae Links to at least two videos of you (1) leading a klezmer ensemble in performance and (2) performing in your main instrument(s), both recorded within the last 5 years II. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Lead 90-minute weekly rehearsals of the Klezmer Ensemble throughout the semester, and direct the Spring concert Assist students with auditions, placement, and enrollment Prepare and distribute a syllabus Assist students with mentorship and musical opportunities as appropriate Submit grades III. SKILLS/ KNOWLEDGE/ CERTIFICATIONS: 1. Required Master’s degree in Music (or Bachelor's degree and equivalent professional experience) Minimum one year prior experience leading a klezmer ensemble Commitment to Mount Holyoke College’s climate of academic excellence and inclusive learning within our gender-diverse women’s liberal arts college environment 2. Preferred N/A   V. SUPERVISION: N/A VI. EDUCATION: Advanced degree (e.g., MA, MS, JD, PhD) Alternatives to formal education and paid work experience may be considered as equivalent qualifications to include military service/training, volunteering, activism, and other non-traditional programs and experiences related to the position.   VII. PHYSICAL/ MENTAL/ WORK ENVIRONMENT DEMANDS: Must be able to gather, classify, and organize information and work Must be able to concentrate on complex tasks and/or on tasks for prolonged periods of time Must be able to adapt well in the face of workplace stressors (ie. complaints, interruptions, competing priorities) DISCLAIMER: This job description may not be inclusive of all assigned duties, responsibilities, or aspects of the job described, and may be amended at any time at the discretion of the Employer. Background Checks: Mount Holyoke College is committed to providing a safe and secure environment, supported by qualified employees that will allow all of its students, faculty, staff and those associated with them to successfully carry out the mission of the college. As a condition of employment, the College will conduct appropriate background checks for all new hires. Mount Holyoke has designated the Office of Human Resources as the office responsible for ensuring that background checks (CORI, SORI, Credit History, & Driver Credential) are completed and utilized in the hiring process and Five College Office of Compliance and Risk Management as the office responsible for facilitating background checks as articulated in this policy. Special Instructions for Applicants:  Apply online; application materials must include: A   cover letter   summarizing interests and qualifications A complete   resume   or curriculum vitae For faculty positions, statements on mentoring, teaching, and research will also be required. ​It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment."
    }
